That's interesting... it solves the problem without removing the
recover stats ability from unihorns. The problem I see is the
reasoning for _all_ unihorns don't functioning at a certain time due
to the global timeout...

I'm trying to think of more possibilities:
- Every time the unihorn is used to restore stats, a point of
enchantment is removed; after -7 the unihorn disappears. Or it doesn't
work at +0.
- Or it sucks 15 HP (virtually transforming HP into recovered stats).
- Or, better, it sucks MP (so in practice it would be the same as
casting the spell?)
- Or it sucks a level from you (maybe too evil? >:-)

But I'm still fond of the 'recover half the stats' lost points' idea;
its reasoning makes more sense.

